Drop a pending quick suggest when a cursor key moves the caret.

SuggestModel answers the end of a composition with _doTriggerQuickSuggest,
which arms a timer (editor.quickSuggestionsDelay, 10 ms by default) whose
callback opens the suggest list wherever the caret is when it fires. A cursor
key pressed before then moves the caret with source 'keyboard' and reason
Explicit, and with no suggestion session active _onCursorChange let that move
through without touching the timer, so the list opened at the key's
destination rather than where the word ended.

On Android that is the ordinary order, not a race. Chromium keeps an
EditContext composition's range where it was when the page moves the
selection (crbug 379170477), so VSCodroid's keyboard guard
(MainActivity.injectKeyboardGuard) ends a composing word in the same task as
the key that moves the caret, just before the key reaches the editor. End on
a line ending in an identifier, or a trackpad drag down onto one, opened the
list there; the drag's next Down then moved the list's highlight instead of
the caret, and an Enter could accept a suggestion instead of starting a new
line.

An Explicit move with no session now cancels the pending timer. Nothing else
changes. Typing moves the caret with reason NotSet and still arms it, and
deleteLeft is an edit with reason NotSet as well. A move from any source
other than 'keyboard' or 'deleteLeft', a mouse or a tap included, already
cancelled through the early exit above the new block. With a session open an
Explicit move still refilters it. Accepting a suggestion, by Tab or by a tap
on a row, cancels the model before its edit, which arrives from source
'suggest'.

Verified against the built bundle, driven in headless Chromium with an
emulated IME and the keyboard guard installed, beside the bundle without this
patch: End from a composing word leaves no list, three synthetic Downs move
the caret three lines where the first used to open the list and the other two
moved its highlight, and Enter after End starts a new line instead of
inserting a suggestion. Typing, a composition committed in place, Left with a
list open, and Tab or a tap accepting a row behave the same in both bundles.

One note for whoever tidies this later. The return ending the new block looks
redundant, since neither branch below it can match an Explicit move with no
session, and folding the block into that else-if chain is the tidier shape.
It is kept because `this._triggerQuickSuggest.cancel();return` is the token
patches/fingerprints.txt matches to prove this patch reached the packaged
bundle: the condition does not survive minification, and the cancel alone
also occurs in cancel(). If you fold it, move that row to something the new
shape introduces and check the replacement occurs zero times in an unpatched
bundle first.

